# device_mmio_running: Every readable register with a root FIFO running after one NOP, read at its offset, at its alias 0x40000 up, unaligned (rounded down), and through a 64-bit wrap; 0x1018 is read-to-clear, so only the first sweep sees the stamp bit. Then every read-only register and unhandled offset is written with 0xffffffff and a sweep shows nothing moved (the device ignores them).
{"op": "config", "ram": [["0x40000000", "0x4000000"]], "stamp_gpa": "0x40008000", "stamp_slots": 2, "watchdog_s": 30}
